WEBVTT

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.420
Your agent session is a zipper.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.560
Every tool call locks onto its result.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.390
Halfway through a job, your laptop sleeps.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.010
Next morning, the session won’t resume.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.880
And you can’t see why.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.820
You could paste in a result that says it worked.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.670
Session Doctor looks before it touches anything.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.850
It names the problem.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.410
One tool call, with no result.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.770
It leaves the original alone, and repairs a copy.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.310
The new piece tells the truth.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.530
Interrupted.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.170
No result available.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.830
A broken line, or a repeated ID, and it stops for review.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.820
Then you test the resume in your own app.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.080
Session Doctor.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.660
Understand a broken session before you repair it.
